  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef numpy_mutation_trap(arr: list, modify_index: int, new_val: float) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Mutation Trap** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef numpy_mutation_trap(arr: list, modify_index: int, new_val: float) -> dict:\n    orig = np.array(arr, dtype=float)\n    cloned = orig.copy()\n    cloned[modify_index] = new_val\n    return {'original': orig.tolist(), 'modified_copy': cloned.tolist(), 'is_independent': bool(orig[modify_index] != cloned[modify_index])}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
